      "math_academy_id": "e-1504",
      "problem": "Find the $7$th term of the following geometric sequence.\n\n$$\n1, \\: 2, \\: 4, \\: 8, \\: \\ldots\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14204584/assets/653f9ccfe28f5e3630afd30562064f1d790245b227896ea7db2da4265f7bac1a.png)\n\nNotice that the sequence is geometric, with a common ratio of \n\n$$\nr=\\dfrac{2}{1}=2.\n$$\n\nSo, we can get each term by multiplying the previous term by $2.$\n\nContinuing to list terms of the sequence until we get to the $7$th term, we obtain the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14204584/assets/6ae31d38f90d943b5bd802652d0dedd4925351b1ffadd6398d018a1dd4c7f0d3.png)\n\nTherefore, the $7$th term is $64.$",
